---
/**
 * media/embed-group — the bordered cell a run of instruments sits in.
 *
 * This is two elements: `.grid` and `.cell--bordered.cell--12`, the dead theme's
 * names, which `styles/legacy.css` still draws for the migrated pages. They wrap
 * the pair of play.maar.world embeds on the ip-orchestra articles and were
 * written out in both language halves — two copies of a wrapper that carries no
 * words at all, which is the purest form of the thing MW-19 removes.
 *
 * KEPT AS THE THEME'S NAMES rather than rewritten, unlike `families/Collect.astro`
 * which computed the same rules out under honest names. The difference is where
 * the markup sits: the Collect landing left `.prose` entirely, so those rules —
 * all of them scoped `.prose .grid` — stopped applying and had to be replaced. An
 * article body is still rendered inside `.prose`, so here they still apply and
 * reproducing them would be a second spelling of a live rule rather than a
 * replacement for a dead one.
 *
 * When `legacy.css` is finally deleted this file changes once, instead of every
 * article that ever held a pair of instruments.
 */
---

<section class="grid">
  <article class="cell cell--bordered cell--12">
    <slot />
  </article>
</section>
